# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  The Best Indeed English Centre — environment
#  Copy to .env.local and fill in. See docs/FORM-SETUP.md for the full story.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Where enrolment requests go ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pick ONE of the two options below.

# OPTION A — Web3Forms (free, 5 minutes, no account beyond an email address).
# Get a key at https://web3forms.com — paste your email, they send the key.
# This key is PUBLIC BY DESIGN: Web3Forms describe it as "an alias to your email
# address". It cannot read submissions or change settings, which is why it is
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. The request is posted from the visitor's browser, because
# Web3Forms answer server-side calls with 403 on the free plan.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# OPTION B — server-side delivery through Resend (https://resend.com).
# Preferred if you want EEA data residency and one processor instead of seven.
# Used automatically when NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY is NOT set.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# ENQUIRY_FROM=The Best Indeed <office@your-domain.md>
# ENQUIRY_TO=founder@your-domain.md

# With neither set, `npm run dev` logs submissions to the terminal instead of
# sending them, so the form can be tested end to end. In production the form
# reports a failure rather than pretending to have sent anything.
